spec:
  type: symmetry/pattern
  grid: 6-10 square; N = 2*(axis_left + 1) so always even
  colors: bg=0, one fg color (any non-zero)
  src:
    description: left half-outline of a horizontally-symmetric closed shape
    location: occupies cols 0..axis_left; cols axis_left+1..N-1 are all bg
    rows: 5-6 consecutive rows, no row gaps; UD symmetric
    per_row: one contiguous fg segment [outer_left..inner_left]
    inner_left_profile: starts/ends at axis_left (cap rows with fill_width=0), non-increasing first half then non-decreasing; step size 1-2
    outer_left_profile: also UD symmetric; step size 1-2 [observed]
    connectivity: 8-connected single component
    cap_rows: exactly 2 (top and bottom), where inner_left == axis_left
    fill_rows: 3-4 interior rows where inner_left < axis_left
    pixel_count: 5-9
  dst:
    description: interior of the completed symmetric shape; outline itself is erased
    per_row: for each fill row, solid fg from inner_left+1 to 2*axis_left - inner_left, LR and UD symmetric
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick N in {6,8,10}; axis_left = N/2 - 1
    2. Build the filled interior (output) as a UD+LR symmetric shape centered at col axis_left+0.5; choose 3-4 fill rows with per-row half-widths forming a non-decreasing-then-non-increasing profile (step 1-2); widths in 1..axis_left
    3. Derive the input outline from the output -- for each fill row, inner_left = axis_left - half_width; place contiguous fg from outer_left to inner_left where outer_left is determined by 8-connectivity with adjacent rows (may equal inner_left or be less); add cap rows at top and bottom with inner_left = axis_left
    4. Verify 8-connectivity of outline; place outline on N x N bg grid with random vertical offset (0-3 top padding)
    5. Clear the grid's right half to confirm it is all bg; return the input grid
